1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,290
Singapore's next heritage grant window is expected to open on the fourth of March.

2
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:08,450
Here's the budget line applicants often overlook.

3
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:14,750
The National Heritage Board runs two co-funding grants: the Minor and the Major Project Grant.

4
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:20,220
Non-profits, cultural groups and individuals apply through the OurSG Grants Portal.

5
00:00:20,570 --> 00:00:24,710
Because they co-fund, you'll need to show how the rest is financed.

6
00:00:25,210 --> 00:00:30,660
Windows have run twice a year: March to mid-April, and August to mid-September.

7
00:00:31,010 --> 00:00:35,570
Both 2026 windows have closed, so use the months ahead to prepare.

8
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:37,780
Confirm the dates on OurSG.

9
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:42,560
NHB's guidelines set what qualifies, so check with them first.

10
00:00:42,910 --> 00:00:52,760
In practice, access and preservation projects often budget for digitising glass-plate negatives, film strips, fragile books and paper archives.

11
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:56,360
A grant-ready scope answers four things.

12
00:00:56,710 --> 00:00:59,260
What you are digitising, and why.

13
00:00:59,610 --> 00:01:04,260
How it will be captured, to FADGI or Metamorfoze guidelines.

14
00:01:04,610 --> 00:01:06,620
Where the files will live.

15
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:10,920
And how the originals will be stored, to ISO 11799.

16
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:16,760
Micrographics Data can turn your collection into a costed scope to attach to your application.

17
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:19,660
Request a quote at micrographicsdata.com.
